      "content": "the \"small victories\" thing feels kind of fake though. like, if he's truly at the end of his rope, a good cup of coffee or a nice sunset isn't gonna change anything. it just feels like false hope. i feel like the most honest way to write him is to just... stop fighting it. to let him realize that the only way to actually find peace is to just let go of everything. does that make sense for the story? or is it too dark?",
